    ],
    "skyPreset": "golden_alpine_meadow",
    "loreSummary": "The thickest thorn drawn anywhere: 43.9 per cent of this region is bramble, the highest share of the eight bramble regions the world carries, all eight of which are on Wracklow. It is the fuel ground, and the marine terrace behind the beach is one of five stone exposures drawn on the island, every one of them an old shoreline. What is not thorn here is meadow, near enough share for share, and no watercourse crosses either."
  },
